      "text": "First, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\). To do this, we can use the Euclidean algorithm or prime factorization.\n\n**Step 1: Prime Factorization**\n- The prime factorization of \\(18\\) is \\(2 \\times 3^2\\).\n- The prime factorization of \\(42\\) is \\(2 \\times 3 \\times 7\\).\n\nThe common factors of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) are \\(2\\) and \\(3\\). Therefore, the GCD is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\).\n\n**Step 2: Least Common Multiple (LCM)**\n- To find the LCM, we take the highest power of each prime factor that appears in the factorizations.\n- The prime factors of \\(18\\) are \\(2, 3, 3\\).\n- The prime factors of \\(42\\) are \\(2, 3, 7\\).\n\nThe LCM is \\(2^1 \\times 3^2 \\times 7^1 = 2 \\times 9 \\times 7 = 126\\).\n\n**Step 3: Product of GCD and LCM**\n- The product of the GCD and the LCM is \\(6 \\times 126\\).\n\nNow, perform the multiplication:\n\\[ 6 \\times 126 = 756 \\]\n\nThus, the product of the greatest common divisor and the least common multiple of \\(18\\) and \\(42\\) is \\(\\boxed{756}\\).",
